# Separate native default-backend reference and unchanged primary comparison

The preserved original offline v2 analyzer rejected three native-inserted default config keys. This versioned read-only adapter validates exactly those defaults against pinned source and explicit launch config, then runs the unchanged remaining checks. Neither terminal run failed and no raw dictionary or frozen producer changed. Two fresh async/backend-default native processes are descriptive references only. They are not added to the synchronous raw/group ABBA estimator. Both async scheduling and graph backend differ from the matched synchronous native recipe; this is not a single-factor cost comparison or a vendor-best/default-all-settings claim.

All 48 original windows are retained, including 16 warmups excluded from estimates. The failed v1 observer attempt remains a pre-window failure in v4, not a third performance sample. All metrics, per-request TTFTs, all-rank backend/environment snapshots and token comparisons accompany this report.

