All request-level first differences and differing-position counts are retained, including warmups and within-process repetitions. Differing generated trajectories limit attribution of whole-window timing solely to scheduling or backend costs; they are not task-quality verdicts. Async queue2 can already hold future D work at the actor's 32-token ingress boundary. Empty post-window queue/client receipts are outside timing, and native absence of persistent plugin graph counters is not a measured zero.

The frozen supplement was calibrated after N1, before candidate timing. Its >100ms and maximum-gap observations do not replace primary P99, establish HTTP Goodput/capacity, or provide pooled-token significance. Quality is assessed by the separate fixed task-quality protocol; native-relative failures remain unchanged. No profile or physical-overlap conclusion is supplied here.
